# RangeLegend

Splits a numeric range into `num_steps` buckets and paints each bucket with a
color from `color_ramp`. Transitions between buckets are hard edges.

```python
from django_map_libre.map import RangeLegend

RangeLegend(
    id="area",
    label="Area",
    coloring_property="area_sqft",
    num_steps=5,
    bounds=(2000, 8000),
    color_ramp=["#0000FF", "#00FF00", "#FF0000"],
    active=True,
)
```

## Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `id` | `str` | Unique identifier inside the overlay. |
| `label` | `str` | Text shown in the legend selector. |
| `coloring_property` | `str` | Numeric feature property driving the buckets. Required. |
| `num_steps` | `int \| None` | Number of buckets. Required unless `config_url` is set. |
| `bounds` | `tuple[float, float] \| None` | `(min, max)` of the range. Inferred from the data when omitted. |
| `color_ramp` | `list[str] \| None` | Ordered list of hex colors. Generated by the frontend when omitted. |
| `config_url` | `str \| None` | URL returning `numSteps`, `bounds` and `colorRamp`. |
| `active` | `bool` | Whether this legend is the rendered one. |

## Local configuration

`num_steps` is required and must be greater than 1. `bounds` and `color_ramp`
are optional:

```python
RangeLegend(
    id="score",
    label="Score",
    coloring_property="score",
    num_steps=11,
    color_ramp=["#FF0000", "#E1FF00", "#00FF1A"],
    active=True,
)
```

When `bounds` is omitted, the frontend computes the min and max of
`coloring_property` from the loaded features. This means the legend is only
rendered after the overlay has finished loading.

## Remote configuration

When `config_url` is set, `num_steps`, `bounds` and `color_ramp` must **not** be
provided. The endpoint must return:

```json
{
  "numSteps": 5,
  "bounds": { "min": 0, "max": 100 },
  "colorRamp": ["#0000FF", "#00FF00", "#FF0000"]
}
```

```python
RangeLegend(
    id="area-api",
    label="Area",
    coloring_property="area_sqft",
    config_url="/api/legend/range",
    active=True,
)
```
